  "answer": "I'll look through the product special-price path and how the storefront decides whether a discount is active.Special prices that included an end date never reached the storefront as a discount. The admin product mapper wrote the end date into the start-date field, and the catalogue price calculation then required the start date to be both before and after today, so a dated special was never applied. The end date is now stored on the special end date, and the price check treats the special as active when the start date is in the past (or absent) and the end date is still in the future. Undated specials are unchanged.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsDiscountTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\", \"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": \"live admin and storefront HTTP APIs\", \"missing\": \"an integration fixture that creates a product through the admin REST API and reads it from the storefront API\"}",
